@startuml
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

component "Client_adapter\nGateway_ipc_binding_client" as client
component "Server_adapter\nGateway_ipc_binding_server" as server
component "Provider_service_binding\nC++" as provider
component "Consumer_service_binding\nC++" as consumer
component "Someipd_service_binding\nC++" as sdsvc
component "SOCom runtime\nC++" as runtime
component "mw::com\nGeneric for bridged services,\ntyped for SomeipdService" as mwcom

note bottom of client
  create_client(): sets up all services eagerly
  and consumes SomeipdService.
  is_connected() follows the SomeipdService proxy.
  Owns one Service_binding per configured service
  instance plus one Someipd_service_binding.
end note

note bottom of server
  create_server(): setup deferred to start(),
  which provides SomeipdService first.
  Owns the same set of bindings as Client_adapter,
  bridged services are symmetric.
end note

note bottom of sdsvc
  Typed skeleton / proxy, not generic, so it
  can carry methods and fields later.
  Provided by someipd, consumed by gatewayd.
  Replaces the Connect / Connect_reply handshake.
end note

note bottom of provider
  Owns GenericSkeleton, per-event in-flight
  allocation table and a SOCom Client_connector.
  Offers while the local service is available.
end note

note bottom of consumer
  Owns FindServiceHandle, GenericProxy and a
  SOCom server connector. Enables it while the
  remote instance is found.
end note

client --> provider : Owns
client --> consumer : Owns
client --> sdsvc : Owns (consumer half)
server --> provider : Owns
server --> consumer : Owns
server --> sdsvc : Owns (provider half)
provider --> runtime : make_client_connector
consumer --> runtime : make_server_connector
provider --> mwcom : Create / OfferService / Allocate / Send
consumer --> mwcom : StartFindService / Subscribe / GetNewSamples
sdsvc --> mwcom : SomeipdServiceSkeleton::OfferService (someipd)\nSomeipdServiceProxy::StartFindService / Create (gatewayd)
@enduml
